  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"1719\" data-end=\"2060\">\n<li data-start=\"1719\" data-end=\"1767\">\n<p data-start=\"1721\" data-end=\"1767\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1721\" data-end=\"1737\">&lt;0.35 kUA/L:</strong> Negative (No sensitization)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1768\" data-end=\"1826\">\n<p data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1826\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1790\">0.35&ndash;0.70 kUA/L:</strong> Low / Doubtful clinical relevance</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1827\" data-end=\"1902\">\n<p data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"1902\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"1849\">0.70&ndash;3.50 kUA/L:</strong> Moderate sensitization (possible clinical allergy)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1903\" data-end=\"1973\">\n<p data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"1973\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"1926\">3.50&ndash;17.50 kUA/L:</strong> High sensitization (likely clinical allergy)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1974\" data-end=\"2060\">\n<p data-start=\"1976\" data-end=\"2060\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1976\" data-end=\"1993\">&gt;17.50 kUA/L:</strong> Very high sensitization (strong likelihood of clinical symptoms)</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
